{
  "1-1": {
    "title": "Fluently add, subtract, and multiply decimals",
    "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.1",
    "learn": "HOW TO ADD, SUBTRACT, AND MULTIPLY DECIMALS\n\nAdding and subtracting: line up the decimal points so place values match. Multiplying: ignore the decimals, multiply like whole numbers, then count decimal places.\n\nExample 1 — Add 3.4 + 5.27\nStep 1: Line up the decimal points and add a zero so both have the same length:\n  3.40\n+ 5.27\nStep 2: Add column by column, right to left: 0+7=7, 4+2=6, 3+5=8.\nStep 3: Bring the decimal point straight down.\nAnswer: 3.4 + 5.27 = 8.67\n\nExample 2 — Subtract 12.5 - 4.83\nStep 1: Line up and add a zero: 12.50 - 4.83.\nStep 2: Subtract right to left, borrowing when needed:\n  12.50\n-  4.83\nStep 3: 0-3 needs a borrow (10-3=7), 4-8 needs a borrow (14-8=6... after borrows), giving 7.67.\nAnswer: 12.5 - 4.83 = 7.67\n\nExample 3 — Multiply 0.6 x 0.7\nStep 1: Ignore the decimals and multiply the digits: 6 x 7 = 42.\nStep 2: Count the total decimal places in BOTH numbers: 0.6 has 1, 0.7 has 1, so 2 places total.\nStep 3: Place the decimal point so the answer has 2 decimal places: 0.42.\nAnswer: 0.6 x 0.7 = 0.42",
    "questions": [
      { "id": "1-1-q1", "section": "math", "question": "Add: 3.4 + 5.27", "choices": { "A": "8.31", "B": "8.67", "C": "8.61", "D": "9.27" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "Line up the decimals: 3.40 + 5.27. Adding gives 8.67.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.1", "difficulty": "easy" },
      { "id": "1-1-q2", "section": "math", "question": "Subtract: 12.5 - 4.83", "choices": { "A": "8.67", "B": "7.67", "C": "8.33", "D": "7.33" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "Line up as 12.50 - 4.83. Subtracting gives 7.67.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.1", "difficulty": "medium" },
      { "id": "1-1-q3", "section": "math", "question": "Multiply: 0.6 x 0.7", "choices": { "A": "4.2", "B": "0.13", "C": "0.42", "D": "0.042" }, "correctAnswer": "C", "explanation": "6 x 7 = 42, and there are 2 decimal places total, so 0.42.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.1", "difficulty": "easy" },
      { "id": "1-1-q4", "section": "math", "question": "Multiply: 1.2 x 0.05", "choices": { "A": "0.6", "B": "0.06", "C": "0.006", "D": "6.0" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "12 x 5 = 60, with 3 decimal places total: 0.060 = 0.06.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.1", "difficulty": "hard" },
      { "id": "1-1-q5", "section": "math", "question": "Add: 4.25 + 0.7", "choices": { "A": "4.32", "B": "4.95", "C": "5.25", "D": "11.25" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "Line up as 4.25 + 0.70 = 4.95.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.1", "difficulty": "easy" },
      { "id": "1-1-q6", "section": "math", "question": "Subtract: 9 - 2.6", "choices": { "A": "6.4", "B": "7.4", "C": "6.6", "D": "5.4" }, "correctAnswer": "A", "explanation": "Write 9 as 9.0, then 9.0 - 2.6 = 6.4.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.1", "difficulty": "easy" },
      { "id": "1-1-q7", "section": "math", "question": "Multiply: 0.3 x 0.3", "choices": { "A": "0.9", "B": "0.6", "C": "0.09", "D": "0.009" }, "correctAnswer": "C", "explanation": "3 x 3 = 9, with 2 decimal places total: 0.09.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.1", "difficulty": "medium" },
      { "id": "1-1-q8", "section": "math", "question": "Multiply: 2.5 x 4", "choices": { "A": "1.0", "B": "10", "C": "100", "D": "8.5" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "25 x 4 = 100, with 1 decimal place: 10.0 = 10.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.1", "difficulty": "medium" },
      { "id": "1-1-q9", "section": "math", "question": "Subtract: 8.07 - 3.9", "choices": { "A": "4.17", "B": "5.17", "C": "4.97", "D": "4.07" }, "correctAnswer": "A", "explanation": "Line up as 8.07 - 3.90 = 4.17.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.1", "difficulty": "hard" },
      { "id": "1-1-q10", "section": "math", "question": "Multiply: 1.5 x 1.5", "choices": { "A": "2.25", "B": "3.0", "C": "1.25", "D": "22.5" }, "correctAnswer": "A", "explanation": "15 x 15 = 225, with 2 decimal places total: 2.25.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.1", "difficulty": "medium" }
    ]
  },
  "1-2": {
    "title": "Fluently divide whole numbers and decimals",
    "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.1",
    "learn": "HOW TO DIVIDE WHOLE NUMBERS AND DECIMALS\n\nWhen dividing by a decimal, move the decimal point in the divisor (the number you divide BY) until it is a whole number. Move the decimal in the dividend the SAME number of places. Then divide.\n\nExample 1 — Divide 144 / 12\nStep 1: Both are whole numbers, so divide directly.\nStep 2: 12 x 12 = 144.\nAnswer: 144 / 12 = 12\n\nExample 2 — Divide 6.4 / 0.8\nStep 1: The divisor 0.8 has 1 decimal place. Move the point 1 place to make it 8.\nStep 2: Move the dividend's point 1 place too: 6.4 becomes 64.\nStep 3: Now divide 64 / 8 = 8.\nAnswer: 6.4 / 0.8 = 8\n\nExample 3 — Divide 0.9 / 0.03\nStep 1: The divisor 0.03 has 2 decimal places. Move the point 2 places to make it 3.\nStep 2: Move the dividend 2 places: 0.9 becomes 90.\nStep 3: Divide 90 / 3 = 30.\nAnswer: 0.9 / 0.03 = 30",
    "questions": [
      { "id": "1-2-q1", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 144 / 12", "choices": { "A": "11", "B": "12", "C": "13", "D": "14" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "12 x 12 = 144, so 144 / 12 = 12.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.1", "difficulty": "easy" },
      { "id": "1-2-q2", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 6.4 / 0.8", "choices": { "A": "0.8", "B": "8", "C": "80", "D": "0.08" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "Move both decimals 1 place: 64 / 8 = 8.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.1", "difficulty": "medium" },
      { "id": "1-2-q3", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 12.5 / 0.5", "choices": { "A": "2.5", "B": "25", "C": "250", "D": "6.25" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "Move both decimals 1 place: 125 / 5 = 25.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.1", "difficulty": "medium" },
      { "id": "1-2-q4", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 0.9 / 0.03", "choices": { "A": "3", "B": "0.3", "C": "30", "D": "300" }, "correctAnswer": "C", "explanation": "Move both decimals 2 places: 90 / 3 = 30.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.1", "difficulty": "hard" },
      { "id": "1-2-q5", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 7.2 / 6", "choices": { "A": "1.2", "B": "12", "C": "0.12", "D": "1.02" }, "correctAnswer": "A", "explanation": "72 / 6 = 12, keep 1 decimal place: 1.2.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.1", "difficulty": "easy" },
      { "id": "1-2-q6", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 250 / 4", "choices": { "A": "62", "B": "62.5", "C": "60.5", "D": "63" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "4 x 62 = 248, remainder 2; 2/4 = 0.5, so 62.5.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.1", "difficulty": "medium" },
      { "id": "1-2-q7", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 3.6 / 0.12", "choices": { "A": "3", "B": "0.3", "C": "30", "D": "300" }, "correctAnswer": "C", "explanation": "Move both decimals 2 places: 360 / 12 = 30.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.1", "difficulty": "hard" },
      { "id": "1-2-q8", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 100 / 0.25", "choices": { "A": "4", "B": "25", "C": "40", "D": "400" }, "correctAnswer": "D", "explanation": "Move both decimals 2 places: 10000 / 25 = 400.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.1", "difficulty": "hard" },
      { "id": "1-2-q9", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 5.6 / 7", "choices": { "A": "0.8", "B": "8", "C": "0.08", "D": "1.8" }, "correctAnswer": "A", "explanation": "56 / 7 = 8, keep 1 decimal place: 0.8.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.1", "difficulty": "easy" },
      { "id": "1-2-q10", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 0.84 / 0.4", "choices": { "A": "21", "B": "2.1", "C": "0.21", "D": "2.4" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "Move both decimals 1 place: 8.4 / 4 = 2.1.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.1", "difficulty": "medium" }
    ]
  },
  "1-3": {
    "title": "Multiply fractions",
    "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2",
    "learn": "HOW TO MULTIPLY FRACTIONS\n\nMultiply the top numbers (numerators) together and the bottom numbers (denominators) together. Then simplify. You do NOT need a common denominator.\n\nExample 1 — Multiply 2/3 x 3/4\nStep 1: Multiply numerators: 2 x 3 = 6.\nStep 2: Multiply denominators: 3 x 4 = 12.\nStep 3: This gives 6/12. Simplify by dividing top and bottom by 6.\nAnswer: 2/3 x 3/4 = 1/2\n\nExample 2 — Multiply 3/4 x 2/9\nStep 1: Numerators: 3 x 2 = 6.\nStep 2: Denominators: 4 x 9 = 36.\nStep 3: 6/36 simplifies (divide by 6) to 1/6.\nAnswer: 3/4 x 2/9 = 1/6\n\nExample 3 — Find 2/3 of 9\n'Of' means multiply. Write 9 as 9/1.\nStep 1: Numerators: 2 x 9 = 18.\nStep 2: Denominators: 3 x 1 = 3.\nStep 3: 18/3 = 6.\nAnswer: 2/3 of 9 = 6",
    "questions": [
      { "id": "1-3-q1", "section": "math", "question": "Multiply: 2/3 x 3/4", "choices": { "A": "1/2", "B": "5/7", "C": "6/7", "D": "2/4" }, "correctAnswer": "A", "explanation": "2x3=6 over 3x4=12, and 6/12 simplifies to 1/2.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "easy" },
      { "id": "1-3-q2", "section": "math", "question": "Multiply: 1/2 x 4/5", "choices": { "A": "5/7", "B": "2/5", "C": "4/10", "D": "1/5" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "1x4=4 over 2x5=10, and 4/10 simplifies to 2/5.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "easy" },
      { "id": "1-3-q3", "section": "math", "question": "Multiply: 3/4 x 2/9", "choices": { "A": "5/13", "B": "6/13", "C": "1/6", "D": "5/36" }, "correctAnswer": "C", "explanation": "3x2=6 over 4x9=36, and 6/36 simplifies to 1/6.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "medium" },
      { "id": "1-3-q4", "section": "math", "question": "Multiply: 5/6 x 3/10", "choices": { "A": "1/4", "B": "8/16", "C": "15/16", "D": "1/2" }, "correctAnswer": "A", "explanation": "5x3=15 over 6x10=60, and 15/60 simplifies to 1/4.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "hard" },
      { "id": "1-3-q5", "section": "math", "question": "Multiply: 2/7 x 7/8", "choices": { "A": "9/15", "B": "1/4", "C": "14/15", "D": "1/8" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "2x7=14 over 7x8=56, and 14/56 simplifies to 1/4.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "medium" },
      { "id": "1-3-q6", "section": "math", "question": "Multiply: 3/5 x 10", "choices": { "A": "13/5", "B": "30", "C": "6", "D": "3/50" }, "correctAnswer": "C", "explanation": "Write 10 as 10/1: 3x10=30 over 5x1=5, and 30/5 = 6.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "medium" },
      { "id": "1-3-q7", "section": "math", "question": "Multiply: 1/3 x 1/3", "choices": { "A": "2/6", "B": "1/6", "C": "2/3", "D": "1/9" }, "correctAnswer": "D", "explanation": "1x1=1 over 3x3=9, which is 1/9.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "easy" },
      { "id": "1-3-q8", "section": "math", "question": "Multiply: 4/9 x 3/8", "choices": { "A": "1/6", "B": "7/17", "C": "12/17", "D": "7/72" }, "correctAnswer": "A", "explanation": "4x3=12 over 9x8=72, and 12/72 simplifies to 1/6.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "hard" },
      { "id": "1-3-q9", "section": "math", "question": "Multiply: 7/10 x 5/14", "choices": { "A": "12/24", "B": "1/4", "C": "35/24", "D": "1/2" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "7x5=35 over 10x14=140, and 35/140 simplifies to 1/4.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "hard" },
      { "id": "1-3-q10", "section": "math", "question": "What is 2/3 of 9?", "choices": { "A": "6", "B": "3", "C": "18", "D": "11/3" }, "correctAnswer": "A", "explanation": "'Of' means multiply: 2/3 x 9 = 18/3 = 6.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "medium" }
    ]
  },
  "1-4": {
    "title": "Understand division with fractions",
    "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2",
    "learn": "UNDERSTANDING DIVISION WITH FRACTIONS\n\nDividing asks 'how many of these fit?' Dividing by a fraction means flipping that fraction (using its reciprocal) and multiplying.\n\nExample 1 — How many 1/2 cups fit in 4 cups?  (4 / (1/2))\nStep 1: Each whole cup holds two 1/2 cups.\nStep 2: So 4 cups hold 4 x 2 = 8 halves.\nStep 3: Check with reciprocals: 4 / (1/2) = 4 x 2/1 = 8.\nAnswer: 4 / (1/2) = 8\n\nExample 2 — Find the reciprocal of 2/5\nStep 1: The reciprocal flips the numerator and denominator.\nStep 2: 2/5 flipped is 5/2.\nAnswer: The reciprocal of 2/5 is 5/2\n\nExample 3 — How many 1/3 pieces are in 6?  (6 / (1/3))\nStep 1: Each whole has three 1/3 pieces.\nStep 2: 6 wholes have 6 x 3 = 18 pieces.\nStep 3: Check: 6 / (1/3) = 6 x 3/1 = 18.\nAnswer: 6 / (1/3) = 18",
    "questions": [
      { "id": "1-4-q1", "section": "math", "question": "How many 1/2 cups are in 4 cups?  (4 / (1/2))", "choices": { "A": "2", "B": "4", "C": "8", "D": "1/8" }, "correctAnswer": "C", "explanation": "Each cup holds two halves, so 4 x 2 = 8. Reciprocal: 4 x 2/1 = 8.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "easy" },
      { "id": "1-4-q2", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 3 / (1/4)", "choices": { "A": "12", "B": "3/4", "C": "7", "D": "4/3" }, "correctAnswer": "A", "explanation": "3 x 4/1 = 12. There are 12 fourths in 3.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "easy" },
      { "id": "1-4-q3", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 6 / (1/3)", "choices": { "A": "2", "B": "9", "C": "18", "D": "1/18" }, "correctAnswer": "C", "explanation": "6 x 3/1 = 18. There are 18 thirds in 6.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "medium" },
      { "id": "1-4-q4", "section": "math", "question": "What is the reciprocal of 2/5?", "choices": { "A": "2/5", "B": "5/2", "C": "-2/5", "D": "10" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "Flip numerator and denominator: 2/5 becomes 5/2.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "easy" },
      { "id": "1-4-q5", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 2 / (1/8)", "choices": { "A": "4", "B": "1/4", "C": "10", "D": "16" }, "correctAnswer": "D", "explanation": "2 x 8/1 = 16. There are 16 eighths in 2.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "medium" },
      { "id": "1-4-q6", "section": "math", "question": "How many 1/4 pieces are in 2 wholes?", "choices": { "A": "6", "B": "8", "C": "2", "D": "1/8" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "Each whole has four fourths, so 2 x 4 = 8.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "easy" },
      { "id": "1-4-q7", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 5 / (1/2)", "choices": { "A": "2.5", "B": "5", "C": "10", "D": "1/10" }, "correctAnswer": "C", "explanation": "5 x 2/1 = 10. There are 10 halves in 5.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "medium" },
      { "id": "1-4-q8", "section": "math", "question": "What is the reciprocal of 7?", "choices": { "A": "7", "B": "1/7", "C": "-7", "D": "14" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "Write 7 as 7/1, then flip it to get 1/7.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "medium" },
      { "id": "1-4-q9", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 1 / (1/6)", "choices": { "A": "1/6", "B": "6", "C": "1", "D": "7" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "1 x 6/1 = 6. There are 6 sixths in 1 whole.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "easy" },
      { "id": "1-4-q10", "section": "math", "question": "Why does dividing by 1/4 give a bigger number than the start?", "choices": { "A": "Because you multiply by the reciprocal 4, and many small pieces fit in each whole", "B": "Because dividing always makes numbers bigger", "C": "Because 1/4 equals 4", "D": "Because you add 4 each time" }, "correctAnswer": "A", "explanation": "Dividing by 1/4 means multiplying by its reciprocal 4, and there are 4 small fourths in each whole, so the count grows.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "hard" }
    ]
  },
  "1-5": {
    "title": "Divide fractions by fractions",
    "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2",
    "learn": "HOW TO DIVIDE A FRACTION BY A FRACTION (KEEP-CHANGE-FLIP)\n\nKeep the first fraction, Change the divide sign to multiply, and Flip the second fraction. Then multiply across and simplify.\n\nExample 1 — Divide 1/2 / 1/4\nStep 1: Keep 1/2.\nStep 2: Change / to x.\nStep 3: Flip 1/4 to 4/1.\nStep 4: Multiply: 1/2 x 4/1 = 4/2 = 2.\nAnswer: 1/2 / 1/4 = 2\n\nExample 2 — Divide 2/3 / 1/6\nStep 1: Keep 2/3, Change to x, Flip 1/6 to 6/1.\nStep 2: Multiply: 2/3 x 6/1 = 12/3 = 4.\nAnswer: 2/3 / 1/6 = 4\n\nExample 3 — Divide 2/5 / 4/5\nStep 1: Keep 2/5, Change to x, Flip 4/5 to 5/4.\nStep 2: Multiply: 2/5 x 5/4 = 10/20.\nStep 3: Simplify 10/20 to 1/2.\nAnswer: 2/5 / 4/5 = 1/2",
    "questions": [
      { "id": "1-5-q1", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 1/2 / 1/4", "choices": { "A": "1/8", "B": "2", "C": "1/2", "D": "4" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "Keep-Change-Flip: 1/2 x 4/1 = 4/2 = 2.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "easy" },
      { "id": "1-5-q2", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 2/3 / 1/6", "choices": { "A": "1/9", "B": "2", "C": "4", "D": "1/4" }, "correctAnswer": "C", "explanation": "2/3 x 6/1 = 12/3 = 4.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "medium" },
      { "id": "1-5-q3", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 3/4 / 1/8", "choices": { "A": "3/32", "B": "6", "C": "3", "D": "1/6" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "3/4 x 8/1 = 24/4 = 6.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "medium" },
      { "id": "1-5-q4", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 5/6 / 5/12", "choices": { "A": "1/2", "B": "25/72", "C": "2", "D": "10" }, "correctAnswer": "C", "explanation": "5/6 x 12/5 = 60/30 = 2.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "hard" },
      { "id": "1-5-q5", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 2/5 / 4/5", "choices": { "A": "1/2", "B": "8/25", "C": "2", "D": "8/10" }, "correctAnswer": "A", "explanation": "2/5 x 5/4 = 10/20 = 1/2.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "medium" },
      { "id": "1-5-q6", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 1/2 / 1/3", "choices": { "A": "1/6", "B": "2/3", "C": "1 1/2", "D": "6" }, "correctAnswer": "C", "explanation": "1/2 x 3/1 = 3/2 = 1 1/2.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "medium" },
      { "id": "1-5-q7", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 3/4 / 3/4", "choices": { "A": "0", "B": "1", "C": "9/16", "D": "3/4" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "3/4 x 4/3 = 12/12 = 1. Any number divided by itself is 1.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "easy" },
      { "id": "1-5-q8", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 7/8 / 1/4", "choices": { "A": "7/32", "B": "2", "C": "3 1/2", "D": "1/2" }, "correctAnswer": "C", "explanation": "7/8 x 4/1 = 28/8 = 7/2 = 3 1/2.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "hard" },
      { "id": "1-5-q9", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 4/5 / 2/15", "choices": { "A": "8/75", "B": "6", "C": "2/3", "D": "3" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "4/5 x 15/2 = 60/10 = 6.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "hard" },
      { "id": "1-5-q10", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 1/3 / 2/3", "choices": { "A": "2", "B": "1/2", "C": "2/9", "D": "1/9" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "1/3 x 3/2 = 3/6 = 1/2.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "medium" }
    ]
  },
  "1-6": {
    "title": "Divide mixed numbers",
    "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2",
    "learn": "HOW TO DIVIDE MIXED NUMBERS\n\nFirst change each mixed number into an improper fraction. Then use Keep-Change-Flip just like dividing regular fractions.\n\nTo make an improper fraction: multiply the whole number by the denominator, add the numerator, and keep the same denominator. Example: 2 1/2 = (2x2+1)/2 = 5/2.\n\nExample 1 — Divide 2 1/2 / 1 1/4\nStep 1: Convert: 2 1/2 = 5/2 and 1 1/4 = 5/4.\nStep 2: Keep-Change-Flip: 5/2 x 4/5.\nStep 3: Multiply: 20/10 = 2.\nAnswer: 2 1/2 / 1 1/4 = 2\n\nExample 2 — Divide 3 1/3 / 1 2/3\nStep 1: Convert: 3 1/3 = 10/3 and 1 2/3 = 5/3.\nStep 2: Keep-Change-Flip: 10/3 x 3/5.\nStep 3: Multiply: 30/15 = 2.\nAnswer: 3 1/3 / 1 2/3 = 2\n\nExample 3 — Divide 4 1/2 / 1 1/2\nStep 1: Convert: 4 1/2 = 9/2 and 1 1/2 = 3/2.\nStep 2: Keep-Change-Flip: 9/2 x 2/3.\nStep 3: Multiply: 18/6 = 3.\nAnswer: 4 1/2 / 1 1/2 = 3",
    "questions": [
      { "id": "1-6-q1", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 2 1/2 / 1 1/4", "choices": { "A": "2", "B": "3", "C": "1 1/2", "D": "4" }, "correctAnswer": "A", "explanation": "5/2 / 5/4 = 5/2 x 4/5 = 20/10 = 2.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "medium" },
      { "id": "1-6-q2", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 3 1/3 / 1 2/3", "choices": { "A": "1 1/2", "B": "2", "C": "3", "D": "5" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "10/3 / 5/3 = 10/3 x 3/5 = 30/15 = 2.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "medium" },
      { "id": "1-6-q3", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 4 1/2 / 1 1/2", "choices": { "A": "2", "B": "3", "C": "6", "D": "4" }, "correctAnswer": "B", "explanation": "9/2 / 3/2 = 9/2 x 2/3 = 18/6 = 3.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "easy" },
      { "id": "1-6-q4", "section": "math", "question": "Divide: 2 1/4 / 1 1/2", "choices": { "A": "1 1/2", "B": "2", "C": "3/4", "D": "3" }, "correctAnswer": "A", "explanation": "9/4 / 3/2 = 9/4 x 2/3 = 18/12 = 3/2 = 1 1/2.", "standard": "MA.6.NSO.2.2", "difficulty": "hard" },
